===Netherlands vs Mexico===
{{further|List of 2014 FIFA World Cup controversies#Netherlands vs Mexico}}
The two teams had met in six previous matches,<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.fifa.com/worldfootball/statisticsandrecords/headtohead/team1=ned/team2=mex/code=-1/index.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140708194850/http://www.fifa.com/worldfootball/statisticsandrecords/headtohead/team1=ned/team2=mex/code=-1/index.html |url-status=dead |archive-date=8 July 2014 |title=Netherlands – Mexico |publisher=FIFA |access-date=28 June 2014 }}</ref> including in the [[1998 FIFA World Cup]] group stage, a [[1998 FIFA World Cup Group E#Netherlands vs Mexico|2–2]] draw. Mexico midfielder [[José Juan Vázquez]] was suspended for the match due to accumulation of yellow cards.<ref>{{cite news |last1=De Menezes |first1=Jack |title=Netherlands v Mexico team news: Robin van Persie returns to lead Dutch as Carlos Salcido replaces suspended José Juan Vázquez for Mexico |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/international/netherlands-v-mexico-team-news-robin-van-persie-returns-to-lead-dutch-as-carlos-salcido-replaces-9571267.html |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/20220501/https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/international/netherlands-v-mexico-team-news-robin-van-persie-returns-to-lead-dutch-as-carlos-salcido-replaces-9571267.html |archive-date=1 May 2022 |url-access=subscription |access-date=26 August 2020 |work=The Independent |date=29 June 2014}}{{cbignore}}</ref>

[[Giovani dos Santos]] opened the scoring for Mexico early in the second half with a left-footed volley from outside the box after gathering a Dutch clearance.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2014/jun/29/holland-mexico-world-cup-2014-last-16-match-report|title=Holland come from behind to snatch last-gasp victory against Mexico|date=29 June 2014 |work=Guardian|access-date=30 October 2014}}</ref>
Mexico led until the 88th minute, when a Dutch corner was headed back by substitute [[Klaas-Jan Huntelaar]] for [[Wesley Sneijder]] to equalise with a hard shot from 16 yards. Only a few minutes later, with stoppage time coming to a close, [[Arjen Robben]] drew a very controversial penalty <ref>{{cite web|url= https://bleacherreport.com/articles/2114007-world-cup-mexico-netherlands-reveals-flaws-in-rules-governing-penalty-kicks|title= World Cup: Mexico vs. Netherlands Reveals Flaws in Rules Governing Penalty Kicks|date=29 June 2014 |work=Bleacher Report}}</ref> for the Netherlands after being fouled by [[Rafael Márquez]] on the right of the penalty area, which Huntelaar converted to win the match for the Netherlands.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Smith |first1=Ben |title=Netherlands 2-1 Mexico |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/27961190 |access-date=26 August 2020 |publisher=BBC Sport |date=29 June 2014}}</ref> Netherlands advanced to the quarter-finals to face [[#Netherlands vs Costa Rica|Costa Rica]], while Mexico were eliminated in the round of 16 for the sixth tournament in a row.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/0/football/27961190|title=Netherlands 2 Mexico 1|publisher=BBC Sport|date=29 June 2014}}</ref>

The match was the first time in World Cup history where a cooling break was instituted, with temperatures at {{convert|32|°C|°F}} and humidity levels at 68%.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.fifa.com/worldcup/news/y=2014/m=6/news=a-cool-first-and-a-historic-triumph-2390305.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140701194754/http://www.fifa.com/worldcup/news/y=2014/m=6/news=a-cool-first-and-a-historic-triumph-2390305.html|url-status=dead|archive-date=1 July 2014|title=A cool first and a historic triumph|publisher=FIFA |date=30 June 2014}}</ref>

