===Costa Rica vs Greece===
The two teams had never met before.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.fifa.com/worldfootball/statisticsandrecords/headtohead/team1=crc/team2=gre/code=-1/index.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140708194854/http://www.fifa.com/worldfootball/statisticsandrecords/headtohead/team1=crc/team2=gre/code=-1/index.html|url-status=dead|archive-date=8 July 2014|title=Costa Rica – Greece |publisher=FIFA |access-date=28 June 2014 }}</ref> This match was Greece's first ever in the FIFA World Cup knockout stage.

[[Bryan Ruiz]] opened the scoring in the 52nd minute when [[Christian Bolaños]] passed to him and he shot low left-footed from outside the penalty area to the right corner of the net with Greek goalkeeper [[Orestis Karnezis]] not moving on his line. Costa Rica were then reduced to 10 men with [[Óscar Duarte (footballer, born 1989)|Óscar Duarte]] being sent off after picking up a second yellow card. [[Sokratis Papastathopoulos]] equalised in injury time shooting into the net from seven yards out after Costa Rica goalkeeper [[Keylor Navas]] had saved an initial shot from [[Theofanis Gekas]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/0/football/27961189 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140630074654/http://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/0/football/27961189 |url-status=dead |archive-date=30 June 2014 |title=Costa Rica 1 Greece 1 (Costa Rica win 5–3 on penalties)|date=29 June 2014 |publisher=BBC Sport |access-date=3 July 2014 }}</ref> No goals were scored in extra time, and the match went to a penalty shoot-out. During the intermission before the penalty shoot-out, the Greek coach [[Fernando Santos (football coach)|Fernando Santos]] was sent off following a dispute with the referee.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://bleacherreport.com/articles/2113881-greece-manager-fernando-santos-sent-off-before-penalty-kicks-vs-costa-rica|title=Greece Manager Fernando Santos Sent off Before Penalty Kicks vs. Costa Rica|date=29 June 2014|access-date=2 July 2014|work=Bleacher Report}}</ref> In the penalty shoot-out, Navas saved Gekas' shot before [[Michael Umaña]] scored the winning penalty for Costa Rica hitting it high to the goalkeeper's right.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2014/jun/30/costa-rica-greece-world-cup-2014-last-16-match-report |title=Costa Rica beat Greece on penalties to meet Holland in quarter-finals|date=29 June 2014|work=Guardian |access-date=3 July 2014}}</ref>

This marked the first time that Costa Rica progressed to the quarter-finals in a FIFA World Cup, where they faced the [[#Netherlands vs Costa Rica|Netherlands]].

