===France vs Nigeria===
{{further|List of 2014 FIFA World Cup controversies#France vs Nigeria}}
The two teams had met in one previous match, in a friendly in 2009, won by Nigeria 1–0.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.fifa.com/worldfootball/statisticsandrecords/headtohead/team1=fra/team2=nga/code=-1/index.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140708194859/http://www.fifa.com/worldfootball/statisticsandrecords/headtohead/team1=fra/team2=nga/code=-1/index.html|url-status=dead|archive-date=8 July 2014|title=France – Nigeria |publisher=FIFA |access-date=28 June 2014 }}</ref>

[[Paul Pogba]] had the best chance in the first half but his right foot volley after a cross from the right was saved by [[Vincent Enyeama]]. In the second half [[Yohan Cabaye]] saw a shot come back off the bar.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2014/jun/30/france-nigeria-world-cup-2014-last-16-match-report |title=France's Paul Pogba rises to occasion to end Nigeria's World Cup hopes |date=30 June 2014 |work=Guardian |access-date=3 July 2014 }}</ref>	The opening goal came with 11 minutes to play when Pogba headed into the net after a mistake by Enyeama where he failed to hold onto a corner kick from the left by [[Mathieu Valbuena]]. In injury time, France got a second when [[Joseph Yobo]] put into his own net under pressure from [[Antoine Griezmann]] after a cross from the right by Valbuena.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/0/football/27969976 |title=France 2 Nigeria 0 |date=30 June 2014 |publisher=BBC Sport |access-date=3 July 2014 }}</ref>

France advanced to the quarter-finals to face [[#France vs Germany|Germany]], while Nigeria were eliminated at the round of 16 in all three World Cups where they reached the knockout stage.

