==Quarter-finals==
===France vs Germany===
{{see also|France–Germany football rivalry}}
The two teams had met in 25 previous matches, including three times in the FIFA World Cup ([[1958 FIFA World Cup|1958]], match for third place: France 6–3 West Germany; [[1982 FIFA World Cup|1982]] semi-finals: France 3–3 (aet) West Germany, West Germany won 5–4 on penalties; [[1986 FIFA World Cup|1986]], semi-finals: France [[1986 FIFA World Cup knockout stage#France vs West Germany|0–2]] West Germany).<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.fifa.com/worldfootball/statisticsandrecords/headtohead/team1=fra/team2=ger/index.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20070614055021/http://www.fifa.com/worldfootball/statisticsandrecords/headtohead/team1=FRA/team2=GER/index.html|url-status=dead|archive-date=14 June 2007|title=France – Germany |publisher=FIFA |access-date=3 July 2014 }}</ref>

The only goal came in the 13th minute when [[Mats Hummels]] got ahead of his marker [[Raphaël Varane]] to head Germany into the lead from ten yards out after a free-kick from [[Toni Kroos]] on the left.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/0/football/28051800|title=France 0 Germany 1|date=4 July 2014|publisher=BBC Sport|access-date=8 July 2014}}</ref> [[Karim Benzema]] had a shot in second half injury time from the left which he hit straight at [[Manuel Neuer]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Germany reach World Cup semi-finals as Mats Hummels header sinks France |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2014/jul/04/france-germany-world-cup-2014-quarter-final-match-report |date=4 July 2014 |work=Guardian |access-date=8 July 2014 }}</ref>

Germany advanced to the semi-finals where they would face [[#Brazil vs Germany|Brazil]]. They became the first team to reach four straight World Cup semi-finals, breaking the record of three shared by their predecessor West Germany (1966–1974 and 1982–1990) and Brazil (1970–1978 and 1994–2002). Germany was also guaranteed their 13th top four finish, the most by any nation.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.wsj.com/articles/germany-beats-france-to-move-on-to-fourth-straight-world-cup-semifinal-1404501569|title=Germany Beats France to Advance to Fourth Straight World Cup Semifinal|publisher=Wall Street Journal|date=4 July 2014}}</ref>

