===Argentina vs Belgium===
The two teams had met in three previous matches, including twice in the FIFA World Cup ([[1982 FIFA World Cup|1982]], group stage: Argentina 0–1 Belgium; [[1986 FIFA World Cup|1986]], semi-finals: Argentina [[1986 FIFA World Cup knockout stage#Argentina vs Belgium|2–0]] Belgium).<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.fifa.com/worldfootball/statisticsandrecords/headtohead/team1=arg/team2=bel/index.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20071215002028/http://www.fifa.com/worldfootball/statisticsandrecords/headtohead/team1=ARG/team2=BEL/index.html|url-status=dead|archive-date=15 December 2007|title=Argentina – Belgium |publisher=FIFA |access-date=3 July 2014 }}</ref> Argentina defender [[Marcos Rojo]] was suspended for the match due to accumulation of yellow cards.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://sports.yahoo.com/news/argentinas-rojo-suspended-world-cup-quarters-223407026--sow.html|title=Argentina's Rojo suspended for World Cup quarters|publisher=Yahoo! Sports|date=1 July 2014}}</ref>

The only goal of the match was scored by Argentina forward [[Gonzalo Higuaín]] in the eighth minute, a powerful shot with his right foot from just inside the penalty area after a pass from Di María was deflected to him by Belgium defender [[Jan Vertonghen]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2014/jul/06/argentina-confidence-belgium-world-cup-2014-match-report|title=Argentina's confidence soars after teamwork triumphs over Belgium|date=6 July 2014 |work=Guardian|access-date=30 October 2014}}</ref>
Higuaín had a chance to extend the lead in the second half, but his shot hit the crossbar.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/0/football/28069209|title=Argentina 1 Belgium 0|publisher=BBC Sport|date=5 July 2014}}</ref> Argentina won 1–0 to advance to the semi-finals, where they would face the [[#Netherlands vs Argentina|Netherlands]].

