===Netherlands vs Costa Rica===
The two teams had never met before.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.fifa.com/worldfootball/statisticsandrecords/headtohead/team1=ned/team2=crc/index.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140707053051/http://www.fifa.com/worldfootball/statisticsandrecords/headtohead/team1=ned/team2=crc/index.html|url-status=dead|archive-date=7 July 2014|title=Netherlands – Costa Rica |publisher=FIFA |access-date=3 July 2014 }}</ref> This was the first time [[Costa Rica national football team|Costa Rica]] had reached the quarter-finals of the World Cup. Costa Rica defender [[Óscar Duarte (Costa Rican footballer)|Óscar Duarte]] was suspended for the match, after being sent off in the round of 16 match against Greece.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.fifa.com/worldcup/news/y=2014/m=6/news=miller-injury-doubt-for-costa-rica-2390645.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140630172816/http://www.fifa.com//worldcup/news/y=2014/m=6/news=miller-injury-doubt-for-costa-rica-2390645.html|url-status=dead|archive-date=30 June 2014|title=Miller injury doubt for Costa Rica|publisher=FIFA |date=30 June 2014}}</ref>

After a goalless 90 minutes, which saw [[Wesley Sneijder]]'s free kick hit the post and [[Robin van Persie]]'s shot deflected onto the crossbar by Costa Rica defender [[Yeltsin Tejeda]], the match headed to extra time. In the second period, substitute [[Marco Ureña]] had a shot saved by Netherlands goalkeeper [[Jasper Cillessen]], while Sneijder had another shot hit the crossbar. In added time at the end of 120 minutes, Dutch manager [[Louis van Gaal]] brought on [[Tim Krul]] to replace Cillessen.<ref>{{cite web|url =https://www.theguardian.com/football/2014/jul/06/holland-coast-rica-world-cup-quarter-final-matchreport|title=Louis van Gaal shows golden touch as Tim Krul antics spook Costa Rica|date=6 July 2014 |work=Guardian|access-date=30 October 2014}}</ref>
In the subsequent penalty shoot-out, Krul saved from [[Bryan Ruiz]] and [[Michael Umaña]], while the Netherlands scored all four of their kicks to advance to the semi-finals, where they would face [[#Netherlands vs Argentina|Argentina]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/0/football/28069208|title=Netherlands 0 Costa Rica (Netherlands win 4–3 on penalties)|publisher=BBC Sport|date=5 July 2014}}</ref>

Uzbek referee [[Ravshan Irmatov]] took charge of his ninth World Cup match, breaking the record of most World Cup games officiated, which he previously held jointly with [[Joël Quiniou]] of France, [[Benito Archundia]] of Mexico, and [[Jorge Larrionda]] of Uruguay.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.goal.com/en-sg/news/3999/world-cup-2014/2014/07/06/4939206/uzbekistan-referee-ravshan-irmatov-sets-world-cup-record|title=Uzbekistan referee Ravshan Irmatov sets World Cup record|website=Goal.com|date=5 July 2014}}</ref>

