===Netherlands vs Argentina===
[[File:2014 FIFIA World Cup, Semi final, NED-ARG.jpg|thumb|Line-up of the teams before the match]]
{{see also|Argentina–Netherlands football rivalry}}
The two teams had met in eight previous matches, including four times in the FIFA World Cup: Netherlands won 4–0 in the second group stage of the [[1974 FIFA World Cup]] and 2–1 in the [[1998 FIFA World Cup knockout stage#Netherlands vs Argentina|quarter-finals]] of the [[1998 FIFA World Cup]], Argentina won 3–1 (after extra time) in the [[1978 FIFA World Cup Final|final]] of the [[1978 FIFA World Cup]], whereas a [[2006 FIFA World Cup Group C#Netherlands vs Argentina|group stage]] encounter of the [[2006 FIFA World Cup]] ended in a 0–0 draw.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.fifa.com/worldfootball/statisticsandrecords/headtohead/team1=ned/team2=arg/index.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100608002107/http://www.fifa.com/worldfootball/statisticsandrecords/headtohead/team1=ned/team2=arg/index.html|url-status=dead|archive-date=8 June 2010|title=Netherlands – Argentina |publisher=FIFA |access-date=7 July 2014 }}</ref>

The Netherlands made one change to their starting line-up from their quarter-final, with [[Nigel de Jong]] returning from injury to replace [[Memphis Depay]], while Argentina made two changes, with [[Marcos Rojo]] returning from suspension to replace [[José María Basanta]] and [[Enzo Pérez]] replacing the injured Di María.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.sbnation.com/soccer/2014/7/9/5884867/argentina-vs-netherlands-lineups-team-news-2014-world-cup|title=Nigel de Jong returns for the Netherlands, Enzo Perez replaces Ángel Di María|publisher=SB Nation|date=9 July 2014}}</ref> The match finished 0–0 after extra-time with very little chances as both sides cancelled each other out.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2014/jul/09/argentina-holland-world-cup-semi-final-match-report|title=Argentina win penalty prize to push past Holland and into World Cup final|date=9 July 2014|work=Guardian|access-date=9 July 2014}}</ref> In the penalty shoot-out, [[Sergio Romero]] saved the first penalty from [[Ron Vlaar]] diving to his left and the fifth penalty of the shoot-out from [[Wesley Sneijder]] when he dived high to his right. Argentina scored all of their four penalties to win 4–2.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/0/football/28122293|title=Netherlands 0 Argentina 0 (Argentina win 4–2 on penalties)|date=9 July 2014|publisher=BBC Sport|access-date=9 July 2014}}</ref> [[Maxi Rodríguez]] scored the decisive fourth penalty, shooting to Dutch goalkeeper [[Jasper Cillessen]]'s right to send Argentina into the [[2014 FIFA World Cup Final|final]], where they would face [[#Final|Germany]], while the Netherlands had to settle for the [[#Match for third place|match for third place against Brazil]].

This was the first World Cup semi-final to end in a goalless draw.{{citation needed|date=August 2020}} Argentina won their fourth [[List of FIFA World Cup penalty shoot-outs|World Cup penalty shoot-out]], tied with Germany for most wins, and were involved in their fifth World Cup shoot-out, a record for any nation.

