==Match for third place==
The two teams had met in 11 previous meetings, including four times in the FIFA World Cup: Netherlands won 2–0 in the second group stage of the [[1974 FIFA World Cup]] and 2–1 in the [[2010 FIFA World Cup knockout stage#Netherlands vs Brazil|quarter-finals]] of the [[2010 FIFA World Cup]], and Brazil won 3–2 in the [[1994 FIFA World Cup knockout stage#Netherlands vs Brazil|quarter-finals]] of the [[1994 FIFA World Cup]] and 4–2 on penalties after a 1–1 draw (after extra time) in the [[1998 FIFA World Cup knockout stage#Brazil vs Netherlands|semi-finals]] of the [[1998 FIFA World Cup]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.fifa.com/worldfootball/statisticsandrecords/headtohead/team1=bra/team2=ned/index.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20070618062458/http://www.fifa.com/worldfootball/statisticsandrecords/headtohead/team1=bra/team2=ned/index.html|url-status=dead|archive-date=18 June 2007|title=Brazil – Netherlands |publisher=FIFA |access-date=11 July 2014 }}</ref>

Brazil made six changes in their starting line-up from their semi-final, while the Netherlands made only two, with [[Wesley Sneijder]], who was originally part of the Dutch starting line-up, replaced by [[Jonathan de Guzmán]] after a hamstring injury during the pre-match warm-up prevented him from playing and [[Jordy Clasie]] replacing [[Nigel de Jong]] due to a groin injury.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.sbnation.com/soccer/2014/7/12/5893901/wesley-sneijder-injured-netherlands-brazil|title = Sneijder ruled out, replaced by de Guzmán|date = 12 July 2014}}</ref>

The Netherlands opened the scoring within three minutes, after Van Persie converted a penalty kick awarded for a foul on [[Arjen Robben]] by [[Thiago Silva]]. [[Daley Blind]] extended the lead in the 17th minute, scoring after a [[David Luiz]] headed clearance fell to him inside the penalty area. [[Georginio Wijnaldum]] completed the scoring in second half injury time as he shot home from substitute [[Daryl Janmaat]]'s cross from the right, the ball going in off the Brazilian goalkeeper’s foot.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/0/football/28173517 |title=Brazil 0 Netherlands 3 |publisher=BBC Sport |date=12 July 2014}}</ref>

The Netherlands finished third for the first time in their World Cup history.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://bleacherreport.com/articles/2127609-brazil-vs-netherlands-world-cup-3rd-place-play-off-score-grades-and-reaction|title=Brazil vs. Netherlands: World Cup 3rd-Place Play-off Score, Grades and Reaction|work=Bleacher Report|date=12 July 2014}}</ref> With [[Michel Vorm]]'s participation (who was substituted into the match in second half injury time), the Netherlands became the first team to use all of their 23 players in a World Cup since the finals squads were expanded from 22 to 23 players in 2002.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://nos.nl/wk2014/artikel/674224-wissel-vorm-zorgt-voor-record.html |title=Wissel Vorm zorgt voor record |website=NOS.nl |date=12 July 2014 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140715045526/http://nos.nl/wk2014/artikel/674224-wissel-vorm-zorgt-voor-record.html |archive-date=15 July 2014 }}</ref>

Brazil, who finished fourth for the second time in World Cup history, conceded a total of 14 goals in the tournament, the most they had ever allowed in a World Cup and also the most conceded by any World Cup hosts.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://msn.foxsports.com/soccer/story/netherlands-claim-third-place-in-world-cup-add-brazil-misery-match-report-071214|title=Netherlands add to Brazil's misery, claim third place in World Cup|work=Fox Sports|date=12 July 2014}}</ref> Brazil also became the second team to concede 100 World Cup goals, after Germany.

Van Persie's goal was the 100th goal that Brazil had conceded in the FIFA World Cup and made him the second highest Dutch goalscorer with six World Cup goals along with [[Wesley Sneijder]], [[Arjen Robben]], [[Dennis Bergkamp]], and [[Rob Rensenbrink]], all behind [[Johnny Rep]] on seven.

Lastly, since the beginning of the 21st century, all four World Cups in [[2002 FIFA World Cup knockout stage#Match for third place|2002]], [[2006 FIFA World Cup knockout stage#Match for third place|2006]], [[2010 FIFA World Cup knockout stage#Match for third place|2010]] and 2014 involved the third-place victors scoring three goals.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://uk.eurosport.yahoo.com/news/world-cup-brazil-humiliated-dutch-take-third-190623389--sow.html |title=World Cup – Brazil humiliated again as Dutch take third |work=Yahoo! Sport |date=12 July 2014 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141012045158/https://uk.eurosport.yahoo.com/news/world-cup-brazil-humiliated-dutch-take-third-190623389--sow.html |archive-date=12 October 2014 }}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2014/jul/12/brazilholland-world-cup-2014-third-place-play-off-match-report|title=Holland heap misery on Brazil with World Cup third-place play-off win|date=12 July 2014|work=Guardian |access-date=14 July 2014}}</ref>

